## Overview

`{{name}}` is a TypeScript scaffold for building GitHub workflow automation.
It comes pre-wired with the tooling used across projects:

- **TypeScript** — strict, ESM, with the `@/*` path alias
- **Vitest** — unit tests with coverage thresholds
- **ESLint + Prettier** — linting and formatting
- **Husky + commitlint + lint-staged** — conventional commits and pre-commit checks
- **OpenCode tooling** — `.agents/` rules and skills, `.opencode/commands/` slash commands

## Requirements

- [Bun](https://bun.sh) — installs dependencies and runs the project

## Getting started

```bash
bun install # installs dependencies and sets up the husky hooks
bun run src/index.ts
```

## Scripts

| Command           | Description                            |
| ----------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| `bun run build`   | Type-check the project (`tsc --noEmit`) |
| `bun run lint`    | Lint with ESLint                       |
| `bun run format`  | Format with Prettier                   |
| `bun run test`    | Run the test suite with coverage       |

## Project structure

```text
.
├── .agents/            # Agent rules and skills
├── .husky/             # Git hooks (commit-msg, pre-commit, pre-push)
├── .opencode/          # OpenCode commands
├── src/                # Application source
│   └── index.ts        # Entry point
└── tests/              # Test suite
    └── fixtures/       # Shared test fixtures and setup
```

